  "complexity": 2,
  "title": "Secret-scanner hygiene: replace credential-shaped test fixtures with shapes no detector matches, and document the fixture rule",
  "spec": "GitGuardian reported \"1 secret uncovered\" on PR 19 (head 6ca204e8). The only credential-shaped strings in that range are test fixtures: tests/test_evidence.py (a raw string containing an API_TOKEN assignment with a made-up value, used to prove evidence.make redacts before persisting) and tests/test_jev_boundary.py (a made-up value assigned to `secret` and joined into an API_KEY assignment to prove jev_rank redacts before sending). They are not credentials, but they trip generic detectors on every scan.\nDo:\n1. In both tests build the fixture at runtime so no literal assignment of the form NAME=value with a secret-looking value exists in the source: e.g. compose the key name and the value from separate parts (\"API_\" + \"TOKEN\", value = \"fixture-\" + \"0\" * 24) or read them from a helper `tests/_fixtures.py::fake_secret(label)` that returns a clearly labelled non-secret value with enough length for jev.redact's rules to trigger (the 32+ char hex/base64 rule or the NAME=value rule). The assertions keep proving redaction (the value must be absent from the outgoing payload and present in the untouched input).\n2. Add `.gitguardian.yaml` at the repo root with `paths-ignore` for tests/_fixtures.py only and a comment explaining that test fixtures never contain real secrets and are built at runtime; do not ignore whole test directories.\n3. docs/context-economy/04-jev-boundary.md: add a two-line \"Fixtures\" note (how to write redaction tests without tripping scanners).\nTests: tests/test_jev_boundary.py and tests/test_evidence.py stay green; add tests/test_fixtures.py::test_fake_secret_has_no_literal_secret_shape_in_source (grep the two test files and tests/_fixtures.py for the regex (?i)(api[_-]?key|token|secret|password)\\s*=\\s*['\"][A-Za-z0-9/+_-]{12,} and assert no match). Never quote double-brace placeholder tokens literally. Do not ask questions.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_fixtures.py::test_fake_secret_has_no_literal_secret_shape_in_source passes",
